@startuml binding-replacement
!theme plain
title Legacy readable-token view: R-REBIND: binding replacement for an existing allocation - design only
actor "Authorised renewing principal\nalready in the retained chain" as P
participant "swarma-dispatcher" as D
participant "swarma-credential-broker" as B
database "Receiver journal / bindings / tombstones" as S
participant "Qualified live lease holder\nagent UID / generation" as E
P -> D: explicit current renewal authority for named existing allocation
D -> D: E-rebind: retain original admitted request; re-sign narrowed leaf\ncurrent dispatcher and caller chains; no account recreation
D -> B: fresh revocation.check for exact chains, context prepare
B --> D: not_revoked | revoked | unavailable
break revoked or unavailable
  D -> D: hold existing allocation; no replacement authority
end
D -> B: binding replacement for same UID/generation\nE-rebind effect identity and immutable arguments (intake unpublished)
B -> B: authenticate dispatcher; require verifiable admission class; refuse untrusted;\nrefuse R-ALLSTOP freeze; current ledger, both chains and narrowing;\ncurrent revocations, R-TIME, restore fence; no helper principal
break pre-admission rejection
  B --> D: typed refusal; class/freeze mappings unpublished; no durable receiver intent
  D -> D: retry requires fresh admission; rejection is not pending
end
B -> S: persist admitted intent before mutation
B -> S: remove old binding, retain removal tombstone
B -> B: end every old-binding lease; close old connections
B -> B: before authority creation, repeat class/freeze and fresh checks under state lock
alt class verified, trusted; no R-ALLSTOP freeze; current checks pass
  B -> S: publish fresh binding ID; never two active bindings for tuple
  B -> S: retain result and recoverable current target state before acknowledgement
  B --> D: recorded result and current state
else class/freeze refusal, lapse, revocation or unresolved evidence
  B -> B: no new authority; retain old removal evidence; reconcile same effect
end
opt crash or lost acknowledgement
  D -> B: effect.observe original effect, bind, canonical-argument digest
  B --> D: recorded | pending | rolled_back | not_recorded | unavailable | contradictory
  D -> D: classify by R-OUTCOME; unknown is never automatic replacement
end
E -> B: fresh connection; verify broker UID; renew old lease
B --> E: refuse: old binding's lease ended
note over D,E
  No seamless env or app-server continuation. Explicit park/restart keeps
  the account until a fenced fresh-lease handoff is published/qualified (§18.11).
  Already copied token keeps only vendor lifetime; it is not erased.
  Exact intake/transaction layout unpublished; labels are semantic, no new fields.
  R-LOCK: per-record ownership; no state lock across platform-service calls.
  [[../spec/broker.md#72-creating-and-removing Spec §7.2]]
  [[../spec/broker.md#132-methods R-OUTCOME tables]]
end note
note over D,B
  R-UNTRUSTED applies even to an existing allocation; no trusted default.
  Binding request carries admission class (encoding unpublished, §18.16).
  R-ALLSTOP journaled freeze closes replacement and all lease/renewal delivery;
  explicit recovery only, partial/unknown results keep admission closed.
  Delivered tokens retain vendor lifetime (§15.5); codes/formats unpublished.
end note
@enduml

@startuml binding-replacement-secret-free
!theme plain
title Proposed secret-free view: binding-replacement — inactive
participant "Authorized replacement owner" as D
participant "Broker" as B
participant "Gateway / action service" as G
database "Durable binding / closure evidence" as S
D -> B : same effect identity + fixed replacement parameters
B -> B : current narrowing / generation / class / stop checks
B -> S : retain intent and old removal/tombstone
B -> B : end old-binding service leases; no inherited authority
B -> G : fence old listener/queue/streams/use
G -> S : durable closure / actual effect outcome or UNKNOWN
alt authority and old closure conclusively reconciled
  B -> S : fresh binding with current authority; no widening
  G -> B : fresh service lease; new caller use checks still required
else lost reply, unknown closure or retired generation
  B -> B : stay closed; reconcile original effect, no blind replacement
end
note over D,G
  Service and caller bindings are distinct.
  Recycled UID / repeated label / stale lease cannot target replacement.
  No seamless env/app-server continuation or speculative handoff format.
  Copied/leaked credentials keep vendor validity independently.
end note

legend bottom
  Separate proposed secret-free mode, document revision 1: INACTIVE / UNQUALIFIED.
  Semantic responsibilities only; no new v0 methods, fields, codes or record formats.
  [[../spec/secret-free-mode.md Owning proposed contract and qualification gates]]
endlegend
@enduml
